    <node id="&quot;SHAWNEE HILLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Shawnee Hills is a village in Delaware County, Ohio, United States, with a total area of 0.44 square miles, all land. The population was 681 at the 2010 census."&gt;||</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHAWNEE HILLS CDP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Shawnee Hills CDP is a census-designated place (CDP) in Greene County, Ohio, United States."&gt;||</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;U.S. DECENNIAL CENSUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"U.S. Decennial Census is a periodic population survey conducted by the U.S. government to gather demographic data."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CENSUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"census is an event where population data is collected, specifically mentioned for the year 2000."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2000&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"2000 is the year of the census, marking a specific point in time for data collection."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CDP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CDP is a census-designated place, a geographic area used for statistical purposes, where the population data was collected."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HAROLD CAGLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Harold Cagle is a representative from Oklahoma's 2nd congressional district, with a background in sports and athletics."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OKLAHOMA'S 2ND CONGRESSIONAL DISTRICT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oklahoma's 2nd congressional district is a political district in Oklahoma where Harold Cagle represents the constituents."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SHS is a school where Harold Cagle graduated, likely Shawnee High School."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OBU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"OBU is a college where Harold Cagle was a track star, likely Oklahoma Baptist University."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1936 SUMMER OLYMPICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1936 Summer Olympics is a historical event where Harold Cagle's 4x400 relay team placed second."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BERLIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Berlin is the city where the 1936 Summer Olympics took place."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOE FRANK COBB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Joe Frank Cobb is an actor known for being the original 'fat boy' in the early 'Our Gang' series, born in Shawnee."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHAWNEE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Shawnee is a city in Oklahoma where Joe Frank Cobb was born and where Patrick Cobbs was also born."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TECUMSEH, OKLAHOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tecumseh, Oklahoma is a nearby town where Patrick Cobbs lived, located close to Shawnee."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRO FOOTBALL RUNNING BACK AND SPECIAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"pro football running back and special refer to the roles played by Patrick Cobbs in professional football."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BATTLE OF FALLEN TIMBERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Battle of Fallen Timbers is a historical battle where Native American tribes were defeated by U.S. forces in 1794."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1794&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1794 is the year of the Battle of Fallen Timbers, marking a significant historical event."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATY OF GREENVILLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treaty of Greenville is a peace agreement signed after the Battle of Fallen Timbers, where Native American tribes ceded land to the U.S."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LE GRAND VILLAGE SAUVAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Le Grand Village Sauvage is a French name for a settlement established by Shawnee groups in Missouri."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TECUMSEH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tecumseh is a historical figure, a Shawnee leader who played a significant role in Native American resistance against U.S. expansion."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TECUMSEH'S WAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tecumseh's War is a conflict involving Tecumseh and his followers against U.S. forces."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WAR OF 1812&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"War of 1812 is a major conflict between the United States and the British Empire, involving various Native American tribes."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BENSON LOSSING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Benson Lossing is an artist who created a drawing of Tecumseh in 1848, based on a 1808 drawing."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2,355 PEOPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUMBER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"2,355 people is the total population count as recorded in the census of 2000."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;819 HOUSEHOLDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUMBER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"819 households is the total number of households recorded in the census of 2000."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;705 FAMILIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUMBER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"705 families is the total number of families recorded in the census of 2000."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POPULATION DENSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Population density is a measure of the number of people per unit area, which was 885.0 in the CDP as of the 2000 census."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;4X400 RELAY TEAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TEAM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"4x400 relay team is a track and field team that participated in the 1936 Summer Olympics and placed second."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATRICK COBBS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Patrick Cobbs is a pro football running back and special, born in Shawnee but lived in nearby Tecumseh, Oklahoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATIVE AMERICAN TRIBES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Native American tribes are the groups that were defeated by U.S. forces at the Battle of Fallen Timbers in 1794."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEW UNITED STATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"new United States refers to the newly formed U.S. government that acquired land from Native American tribes through treaties."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MISSOURI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Missouri is the state where some Shawnee groups migrated and settled along Apple Creek after rejecting the Treaty of Greenville."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APPLE CREEK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Apple Creek is a creek in Missouri where some Shawnee groups settled after migrating west of the Mississippi River."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DRAWING OF TECUMSEH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ARTIFACT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Drawing of Tecumseh is an artistic representation created by Benson Lossing in 1848, based on a 1808 drawing."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1808 DRAWING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ARTIFACT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1808 drawing is an original drawing of Tecumseh that Benson Lossing used as a reference for his 1848 drawing."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0144-5345c9ee8364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1848 DRAWING&quot;">
